  "canonical_initialization_order": [
    "Fork CPU and logical CUDA device 0 RNGs; seed both to 1234. Use CUDA default factory device for the following host model construction only.",
    "Construct ordinary ParticlePrior(20000, 2): allocate FP32 on CUDA, then normal_(mean=0, std=1) on CUDA; this discarded draw must be retained.",
    "Redraw prior.z uniform_(-5, 5) on CUDA.",
    "Construct nn.Linear(2, 2) on CUDA: its default weight draw followed by bias draw must occur. Then copy identity weight and zero bias; overwrites consume no RNG.",
    "Construct SimpleMLPDiscriminator(2, 128, 3, fourier=3) on CUDA. Deterministic Fourier buffer precedes Linear layers; then default weight and bias draws for each of Linear(14,128), Linear(128,128), Linear(128,128), Linear(128,1), in that order.",
    "After ALL critic default constructors finish, traverse those four Linear layers in order: xavier_uniform_ each weight, zero each bias. Do not interleave construction and Xavier redraws.",
    "Retain initial prior/G/D tensors and CPU/CUDA RNG receipts, require known prior/G hashes before any update, and compare complete new parameter hashes across survivor hosts.",
    "Restore caller factory-device context; create each candidate through its unchanged public API, preserving its declared optimizer and serial-backward semantics. Do not inject optimizer counters or copy historical noise/LR schedules into the continuing learner."
  ],
